# Secrets — NEVER commit (parity with other PWG / Creative Machines repos)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env
# cut.env is the DELIBERATE exception: it is the committed record of every
# input to a DMG cut (paths + pins + gate bases), holds NO secrets, and is
# useless if untracked -- `git log cut.env` is meant to BE the cut history.
# It was silently swallowed by `*.env` on 2026-08-06; the commit that added
# it reported success while committing nothing.
!cut.env
SERVER_INFO.md
config.local.*
*.pem
*.key
*_private*
*credentials*
*token*
# Vendored Doctor source module (NOT a secret) - the broad *token* guard above
# otherwise swallows it, which dropped it from the vendor and blanked the iOS
# Pairing tab (chat_token.py is lazy-imported by web_ui.py). Keep tracked.
!vendor/doctor/agent/chat_token.py
secrets/
credentials/

# State files (contain user-specific data)
state.json
*.state

# Real-person fixtures / private test directories (per HR015 Rule Zero)
fixtures_private/
conversations/
transcripts/
raw_data/
.pii-blocklist

# Python (if any test harnesses land here)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# W8 / F6: the signed Safari extension .app.zip is a binary build artefact
# produced by CM020's bin/build-safari-extension.sh and staged here by ORM at
# cut time. It is large + signed-per-cut, so it is NOT committed to git; the
# vendor/extensions/ directory is kept tracked via its .gitkeep so the path
# exists for the staging step.
vendor/extensions/OstlerSafariExtension.app.zip

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# User-specific deployment config
deploy.local.yml

# Operator session prompts
AGENT_PROMPT.md
REVIEW_FIXES_PROMPT.md

# Claude Code
.claude/

# Test artefacts
test_installs/
scratch/

# Xcode (gui/) – keep project.yml + sources, drop build output and
# user-specific Xcode metadata. The .xcodeproj is regenerated from
# project.yml via `xcodegen generate` so it doesn't need to live in
# git either, but we DO commit it for now so a fresh checkout can
# `xcodebuild ... build` without needing xcodegen.
gui/build/
gui/dist/
gui/DerivedData/
gui/**/xcuserdata/
gui/**/*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
gui/**/.build/
gui/**/Packages/

# Locally-built daemon binary bundled into the DMG at cut time. NOT tracked
# in source -- built fresh from the ostler-assistant source repo via
# `cargo build --release --bin zeroclaw` + signed + stripped, then copied
# to assistant-agent/bin/ostler-assistant by the operator-facing
# `make ship` runner. The customer-facing GitHub release tarball is the
# durable distribution channel; this bundling is the offline-capable
# fallback that ships in DMG Resources. CX-79b (2026-05-25).
assistant-agent/bin/
# CX-88 (DMG #48g, 2026-05-29): make stage-daemon fetches the v0.4.4 daemon
# tarball from the private ostler-ai/ostler-assistant release and extracts
# the .app bundle here. Bundle phase in gui/project.yml copies it into
# OstlerInstaller.app/Contents/Resources/assistant-agent/OstlerAssistant.app/
# at xcodebuild time. NOT tracked in source -- the tarball is recreated
# on every `make ship` run.
assistant-agent/OstlerAssistant.app/

# F1 hygiene: never bundle stale python-build output (pre-F1 consent_cli)
vendor/ostler_security/build/
**/*.egg-info/
